# Append-only logs: resolve concurrent appends automatically.
#
# `merge=union` is a git built-in — on a three-way merge it keeps BOTH sides'
# lines instead of raising a conflict. These files are journals: two agents
# appending different entries is not a disagreement, and asking a human to
# resolve it every time is a tax on parallel work with no upside.
#
# Line ORDER after a union merge follows merge order, so treat these as a set of
# entries and not a sequence. Anything where order is load-bearing does not
# belong here.
DECISIONS.md merge=union
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
